   "date": "2012-09-11T21:10:03Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] High-dimensional array subset to matrix?",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>On 9/11/12 4:56 PM, Andrew Gelman wrote:\r<br>&gt; It might be a good idea in the manual to have an example like this, in which we format the same array in several\r<br>&gt; different ways, so users can see the equivalencies.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "There is already such a discussion.  More than\r<br>one, in fact.  Check out the section on vectorization\r<br>in the optimization chapter of the user&#39;s guide.\r<br>\r<br>There should probably be a whole section in the user&#39;s\r<br>guide on vectors, row vectors, matrices and arrays.\r<br>One thing that&#39;s not adequately discussed with examples\r<br>is the return type for matrix operations.  It&#39;s all\r<br>fully documented, but I think users coming from R who\r<br>are not used to reading function-signature doc may get\r<br>confused.\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br> &gt; We can then also explain why some parameterizations work more\r<br>&gt; efficiently than others.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
